    <h2>Why people choose implants</h2>
    <p>A gap from a missing tooth can make eating awkward, and neighbouring teeth can slowly drift into the space. An implant replaces the tooth without touching the healthy teeth either side, which a bridge needs to do. It is not the only answer, and we always talk through the others.</p>
    <h2>The stages</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Planning:</strong> the scan, your options, a written plan and costs.</li>
        <li><strong>Placement:</strong> the post goes in, under local anaesthetic.</li>
        <li><strong>Healing:</strong> a few months while the jaw settles around it, often with a temporary tooth.</li>
        <li><strong>The crown:</strong> made to match your teeth, and fitted.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Paying for it</h2>
    <p>Implants are an investment, and we would rather you plan for one than feel pushed. See <a href="/insurance/">insurance and payment</a> for our interest-free monthly plan, and how we check what your insurer may cover before we begin.</p>
